## Frozen training configuration

| Component | Value |
|---|---|
| Base model | `Qwen/Qwen3-8B` |
| Precision | BF16 LoRA; base weights frozen; no quantization |
| LoRA | r=32, alpha=64, dropout=0.05, bias=none, all-linear |
| Optimizer | adamw_torch_fused, learning rate 1e-4, cosine schedule |
| Training | 2 epochs, batch 2, accumulation 8, effective batch 16 |
| Regularization | warmup 0.03, weight decay 0, max grad norm 1.0 |
| Sequence handling | max length 2,048, packing false, completion-only loss |
| Runtime | gradient checkpointing, use_cache=false, seed/data_seed=42 |
| Checkpoint rule | lowest offline validation completion loss only |

Installed additions were limited to TRL 0.23.0, PEFT 0.17.1, and datasets
4.0.0. Existing torch 2.6.0+cu124, transformers 4.56.2, accelerate 1.10.1,
CUDA, and ALFWorld were not upgraded. The allowed 1x16 OOM fallback was not
used.

## Training result

The full run completed 2,354 optimizer steps in 27,406.3 seconds (7.61 hours).
It processed 23,860,000 padded input tokens. All 8,190,735,360 base parameters
remained frozen; 87,293,952 LoRA parameters were trainable (1.0545% of the
combined parameter count). Peak allocated GPU memory was 23,665,892,352 bytes.

| Point | Validation loss | Completion-token accuracy |
|---|---:|---:|
| Epoch 1 / step 1,177 | 0.077733 | 97.13% |
| Epoch 2 / step 2,354 | 0.063817 | 97.42% |

Final aggregate training loss was 0.100513. The preregistered validation-loss
rule selected epoch 2 before online evaluation. The unmerged adapter remains at
`artifacts/runtime/model-artifacts/sft-policy-bootstrap/full/final_adapter`
with SHA-256
`6e403d85b150a74dfcc176f1f180ce4baf6fdacd922d2f96b3ceef0a21100f11`.

The exact clean Git revision before model inference and full training was
`f44ec40b2e12d34cb709b32eca591bae7b39d45d`.

## Offline imitation accuracy

For `N=2,139` task-disjoint expert states, exact accuracy is

`Accuracy = (1/N) * sum_i I[predicted_ID_i = expert_ID_i]`.

| Condition | Exact ID | Exact command | Malformed | Out of range |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Base SFT-P0 | 709/2,139 (33.15%) | 33.15% | 0 | 1 |
| SFT LoRA | 1,933/2,139 (90.37%) | 90.37% | 0 | 0 |

Exact command accuracy maps each predicted ID back through the current
environment-owned map before comparison. The +57.22 percentage-point gain is
imitation evidence, not by itself environment competence.

## Matched online evaluation

The control and SFT policy ran the same 60 reserved train tasks, schedule
positions, nominal seeds 7000-7059, 50-step horizon, SFT-P0 prompt, greedy
decoder, `thinking=false`, 16-token generation budget, strict parser, and
environment action semantics. Exact task/seed/reset matching was verified.

Success rate is `SR = successes / episodes`. For matched binary outcomes,
`net gain = N_01 - N_10`, where `N_01` is base-fail/SFT-success and `N_10` is
base-success/SFT-fail.

| Metric | Base | SFT |
|---|---:|---:|
| Success | 3/60 (5.0%) | 48/60 (80.0%) |
| Mean episode length | 46.95 | 22.58 |
| Fail -> success | - | 45 |
| Success -> fail | - | 0 |
| Net matched success gain | - | +45 |

### Task family success

| Family | Base | SFT | Matched net |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| look_at_obj_in_light | 2/10 | 9/10 | +7 |
| pick_and_place_simple | 1/10 | 10/10 | +9 |
| pick_clean_then_place_in_recep | 0/10 | 9/10 | +9 |
| pick_cool_then_place_in_recep | 0/10 | 9/10 | +9 |
| pick_heat_then_place_in_recep | 0/10 | 10/10 | +10 |
| pick_two_obj_and_place | 0/10 | 1/10 | +1 |

No family had a matched success loss. Pick-two remains the dominant residual
weakness: nine of the twelve SFT failures were partial-progress pick-two tasks.
The other failures were one search failure, one procedural/light-use failure,
and one post-transformation placement failure.

## Funnel and behavior

Funnel milestones are derived only from public observations and executed
actions. Discovery means the target instance appeared in an observation;
acquisition requires an observed pickup; transformation requires the correct
clean/cool/heat outcome; final completion requires the task's final placement
or light-use event.

| Metric (episodes) | Base | SFT | Matched net |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Target discovered | 16 | 59 | +43 |
| Target acquired | 16 | 59 | +43 |
| Correct transformation | 0 | 29 | +29 |
| Final placement/completion | 14 | 48 | +34 |

An adjacent repeat is `I[a_t = a_(t-1)]`. A strict two-cycle event is counted
when a four-action window repeats its preceding two-action pair. Repeated
receptacle navigation is total grounded `go to` events minus unique visited
receptacles. Off-target manipulation counts grounded `take`, `move`, `heat`,
`cool`, `clean`, or `use` actions that reference neither the task target nor
the required light.

| Behavior count | Base | SFT |
|---|---:|---:|
| Adjacent repeats | 588 | 1 |
| Strict two-cycles | 1,504 | 167 |
| Repeated receptacle navigation | 382 | 103 |
| Off-target manipulations | 1,039 | 0 |

## Protocol and cost

Executable validity is `executed grounded decisions / total decisions`.

| Metric | Base | SFT |
|---|---:|---:|
| Decisions | 2,817 | 1,355 |
| Executable validity | 99.9645% | 100% |
| Malformed / out-of-range IDs | 1 / 0 | 0 / 0 |
| Mapping failures | 0 | 0 |
| Wrong-command executions | 0 | 0 |
| Unclassified parser failures | 0 | 0 |
| Mean input tokens/decision | 574.33 | 546.24 |
| Mean generated tokens/decision | 5.0004 | 5.0000 |
| Mean policy latency/decision | 0.2695 s | 0.4266 s |

SFT adds about 0.157 seconds per decision in this sequential run. The first
cold decision was 7.677 seconds for base and 7.268 seconds for SFT, so this run
does not show a positive adapter-specific cold-load penalty. Those cold values
also include base-model loading and are order/cache dependent; they are not an
isolated LoRA loading benchmark.

## Frozen gate

| Requirement | Threshold | Result | Pass |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Executable validity | >=98% | 100% SFT | yes |
| Mapping / wrong-command / unclassified failures | 0 | 0 / 0 / 0 | yes |
| Net matched successes | >=+8 | +45 | yes |
| Absolute SFT success | >=18/60 | 48/60 | yes |
| Maximum family matched loss | <=2 | 0 | yes |

The frozen decision is therefore **A. SFT ESTABLISHES A COMPETENT BASE**.

## Limitations and next step

- This is a train-split development evaluation, not valid-seen or valid-unseen
  generalization evidence. The 60 tasks are now consumed development tasks and
  must not be used for tuning or later held-out claims.
- Behavioral cloning can still suffer covariate shift after self-induced
  mistakes. The large offline and online gains make category C inappropriate,
  but they do not eliminate this risk on new distributions.
- The result is one preregistered LoRA configuration and one deterministic run;
  no hyperparameter comparison or variance estimate was performed.
- Pick-two performance is only 1/10 despite task-balanced training and requires
  analysis before claiming uniformly competent long-horizon control.
- The online latency comparison was sequential and does not isolate adapter
  loading from cache and process-order effects.

The SFT adapter should be frozen as the new base candidate. A future protocol
may first validate it on fresh held-out tasks, then collect a new paired
recovery corpus and measure `V_raw = R_recover - R_continue`. Preference-pair
construction and DPO/ORPO should occur only after that fresh value-density
measurement. None of those later phases began here.

